{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Seven times.</b> On the back of the hand of the metzora." "<b>And he shall cleanse him.</b> By speech." "<b>And he shall send the bird.</b> It is a sign of purification, to banish the tzara'at from him and to make for him a model: for he had sat like a solitary bird on a roof, bound and forbidden from coming together with other people, and now he is permitted to come with his fellows — like this bird, which was bound in a person's hands and is now sent away and free to go with its companions."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:12:08.181744423Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}